Fix three native compatibility bugs in Quickshell v0.3.1.

NetworkManager defaults an omitted Wi-Fi mode to infrastructure. Keep explicit
non-infrastructure modes excluded without changing other profile matching.
An absent Wi-Fi security group means Open; malformed explicit security remains
Unknown rather than being treated as an open network.
Notification action identifiers can be reused with updated display labels.

diff --git a/src/network/nm/wireless.cpp b/src/network/nm/wireless.cpp
--- a/src/network/nm/wireless.cpp
+++ b/src/network/nm/wireless.cpp
@@ -123,9 +123,9 @@

-	const auto ssid = map["802-11-wireless"]["ssid"].toString();
-	const auto mode = map["802-11-wireless"]["mode"].toString();
-
-	if (mode == "infrastructure") {
-		auto* net = this->mNetworks.value(ssid);
-		if (!net) net = this->registerNetwork(ssid);
-		net->addSettings(settings);
+	const auto ssid = map["802-11-wireless"]["ssid"].toString();
+	const auto mode = map["802-11-wireless"]["mode"].toString();
+
+	if (mode.isEmpty() || mode == "infrastructure") {
+		auto* net = this->mNetworks.value(ssid);
+		if (!net) net = this->registerNetwork(ssid);
+		net->addSettings(settings);

diff --git a/src/network/nm/utils.cpp b/src/network/nm/utils.cpp
